5. Refractory hypertension: systolic blood pressure ≥200 mmHg or diastolic blood pressure ≥110 mmHg; hypotension: systolic blood pressure \ 1.5 × upper limit of normal \[ULN\]), renal dysfunction (Cr \>1 × ULN);
7. Coagulopathy (prolonged INR (\>1.5) or prolonged APTT (\>2 folds);
